/*
  core/masks/outcome_policy.spthy -- the human-model OUTCOME MATRIX (agnostic masks, AGNOSTIC_MASKS.md).
  Maps (mask, action-class) -> outcome, the way core/lexicon_tlx.spthy maps action -> demand. This is the
  one place the f_H behaviour knowledge lives; the generic behaviour rules (core/masks/<class>_behavior.spthy)
  read it and bind the mask + outcome, so a ceremony adds no per-action mask files.

  Pilot scope: the COMPUTE action class (collapses the old Calc_* and Op_* masks).
    Attentive + compute -> correct   (produce the genuine value)
    Busy     + compute -> slip       (a fresh wrong value; top symbol != kdf)
    Careless + compute -> timeout    (no response; safe-fail stall)

  Seeded unconditionally so any theory using a behaviour rule stays CLOSED; persistent + read-only ->
  no sources loop (repo MEMORY.md S6.2). OnceOutcomePolicy bounds the seed. As more action classes are
  migrated (compare/confirm/decide/authorize/share), add their rows here -- one table, reused.
*/

rule Seed_outcome_policy:
    [ ]
  --[ SeedOutcomePolicy() ]->
    [ !OutcomePolicy('Attentive', 'compute', 'correct'),
      !OutcomePolicy('Busy',      'compute', 'slip'),
      !OutcomePolicy('Careless',  'compute', 'timeout') ]

restriction OnceOutcomePolicy:
  "All #i #j. SeedOutcomePolicy()@i & SeedOutcomePolicy()@j ==> #i = #j"
